    <!-- ── Configs ▸ Panel ▸ Control ────────────────────────────────────
         The status light on every row, and the page chrome around it. All of
         it is here rather than in ControlFragment.kt because the owner reads
         this app in Spanish: a sentence compiled into Kotlin cannot be
         translated, and this page is the one that says whether the phone and
         the fleet are working. NOTE for whoever adds the first translated
         locale: this app has no values-<lang> at all yet, so these need a
         values-es alongside the other 123 strings, not on their own. -->
    <string name="status_light_on">On</string>
    <string name="status_light_off">Off</string>
    <!-- Nobody has an answer YET: not read, still reading, the call threw,
         the platform declined, or the last answer has aged out. -->
    <string name="status_light_unknown">Unknown</string>
    <!-- Nobody can EVER have an answer from here: the only thing readable is
         a preference this app stored, which is what was asked for and not
         what is true. Never shortened to "Unknown" — the owner can wait out
         an unknown, and waiting out this one would never end. -->
    <string name="status_light_unverifiable">Not verifiable</string>
    <!-- Spoken by a screen reader for one row's light: row name, then state.
         %1$s = the control's label, %2$s = one of the four words above. -->
    <string name="status_light_description">%1$s: %2$s</string>

    <string name="control_title">Control</string>
    <!-- %1$s..%4$s are the four light readings (glyph + word) and %5$d is the
         refresh interval in seconds, so this paragraph cannot describe a
         light the page does not draw. -->
    <string name="control_caption">The things flipped often enough to deserve one screen, laid out as a grid of tiles and grouped by WHAT YOU CAME LOOKING FOR: the handset, the network, the tooling, the interface.\n\nTAP a tile to switch it. HOLD it to open the settings screen behind it — and every tile answers a hold, including the ones with nowhere to go, which say so instead of doing nothing.\n\nA lit tile is inverted: it fills with the theme\'s foreground colour and draws its icon in the background one, so on and off are the same two colours swapped and neither can become invisible under a theme. Only what can really move switches on a tap. A tile Android will not let this app flip opens the system screen that owns it instead, and a tile waiting on a grant says which grant on its label.\n\nBattery Hungers is not a fifth category — it is the SAME tiles again, gathered so everything draining the battery can be switched off in one place. A tile flipped there is flipped in its own group at the same instant, because there is only one of it.\n\nThe light under a tile is what the DEVICE answered just now, never what the tile is set to: %1$s, %2$s, or %3$s when it would not say or has not been asked yet. %4$s marks the tiles where nothing but this app\'s own stored preference can be read. Lights refresh every %5$d seconds while this page is open and stop entirely when it is not, so they go unknown before they go stale.</string>
    <string name="control_none_declared">No controls are declared — build.json::ui.control_panel is empty or did not reach this build.</string>
    <!-- A write the device refused. %1$s = the control's label, %2$s = what
         the re-read reported. -->
    <string name="control_write_refused">%1$s: didn\'t change — %2$s</string>

    <!-- ── Configs ▸ Panel ▸ Control — GROUP HEADINGS ──────────────────────
         Named by build.json::ui.control_panel.groups[].label_res / subtitle_res
         and resolved at render time. They live here and not in build.json
         because the owner reads this app in Spanish and a heading that only
         existed in the declaration could never be translated. The group IDS
         stay in build.json; only the wording is here. -->
    <string name="control_group_device">Device</string>
    <string name="control_group_device_sub">The handset\'s own hardware and attention.</string>
    <string name="control_group_network">Network</string>
    <string name="control_group_network_sub">Everything that moves bytes — this handset\'s radios and the fleet\'s tunnels, in one place.</string>
    <string name="control_group_tools">Tools</string>
    <string name="control_group_tools_sub">The machinery this app and the fleet are driven through.</string>
    <string name="control_group_ui">UI</string>
    <string name="control_group_ui_sub">How this launcher looks and feels under the thumb.</string>
    <string name="control_group_battery">Battery Hungers</string>
    <string name="control_group_battery_sub">The same controls again, gathered so everything draining the battery can be switched off from one row.</string>

