         measured from the notification listener at draw time; none of it is
         declared, and none of it costs a model call. -->
    <string name="inbox_summary_header">SUMMARY · %1$s</string>
    <string name="inbox_summary_apps">Apps</string>
    <string name="inbox_summary_channels">Channels</string>
    <string name="inbox_summary_notifications">Notifications</string>
    <string name="inbox_summary_latest">Latest</string>
    <!-- Shown against Latest when the class is empty. Not "0" and not a blank:
         there is no newest thing, which is a different fact from a zero count. -->
    <string name="inbox_summary_latest_none">none yet</string>
    <string name="inbox_summary_counted">Counted from the phone notification listener at the moment this card was drawn.</string>
    <string name="inbox_summary_channels_note">Channel messages are fetched per channel after this card is drawn, so they are in the boxes below rather than in the count above.</string>
    <string name="inbox_notifications_header">NOTIFICATIONS · %1$s</string>
    <string name="inbox_class_silent">silent · nothing captured in %1$s</string>

    <!-- WHAT MAIL ACTUALLY REACHES. The owner asked for "the summary of all
         mails"; this screen can read mail NOTIFICATIONS and cannot read mail.
         Saying so on the card is the difference between a smaller true claim
         and a larger false one. -->
    <string name="inbox_note_mail">These are mail NOTIFICATIONS, not the mail itself. The messages live in the mail app\'s own store, which this screen does not read — so a mail that arrived silently, or was already dismissed from the shade, is not counted above.</string>

    <!-- Data faults. Both are addressed to the person holding the phone, and
